IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-s73a-d-restraint.l4: sections 73A to 73D (measures for dealing with unmeritorious or vexatious proceedings).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 4372-4769).  The appeal-permission functions take the court of s 29C as an input
-- (seam 9 of PLAN.md: `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`) and pass NOTHING through.
-- "A court" is the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (s 2, "court"); the Singapore International Commercial Court
-- is counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1); the Family Division of the High Court answers NOTHING (undefined term) and every subordinate court answers JUST FALSE (s 2 "court" means three named courts; fork S3-B1).
-- The 2-year caps of ss 73C(4)(a), 73C(5)(b), 73D(4)(a) and 73D(5)(b) compare two dates: a period of exactly 2 years from a day ends on the day before the second anniversary
-- (fork; the staged Interpretation Act module has no counting rule for years, so it is not imported).

§ `Sections 73A to 73D: civil restraint orders and other measures`

-- src:381 | “court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division, or
-- src:382 | the Court of Appeal;
@ref s 2 "court" (src:381-382)
-- A court within the section: the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal.
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A the court is a court within the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- the Singapore International Commercial Court is a division of the General Division (s 18A); counted with it through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): s 2 defines "court" as the General Division, the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, and nothing here says whether the Family Division of the High Court is part of the General Division
    WHEN `Family Division of the High Court` THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 2 "“court” means the General Division, the Appellate Division, or the Court of Appeal", and a subordinate court is not among them (fork S3-B1; the opening "unless the context otherwise requires" is the marginal reading)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4416 | (4) The General Division may, in respect of any legal proceedings
-- src:4417 | in any subordinate court —
@ref s 73A(4) ("The General Division") (src:4416-4417)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A the court is the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision names "the General Division" and no other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Helper: an answer that holds only where the court is within the section; where the gate says the court is not one, the answer is no.
GIVEN gate IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN answer
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the gate answered no, which for the gate of s 2 "court" is that "court" means the General Division, the Appellate Division, or the Court of Appeal
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4382 | 73A.—(1) A court may, in respect of any legal proceedings in the
-- src:4383 | court —
-- src:4385 | (a) make a limited civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4386 | section 73B;
-- src:4388 | (b) make an extended civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4389 | section 73C; or
-- src:4391 | (c) make a general civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4392 | section 73D.
@ref s 73A(1) (src:4382-4392)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(1) the court may make a limited, extended or general civil restraint order in respect of the legal proceedings` MEANS
    -- the conditions of each kind of order are those of ss 73B, 73C and 73D
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "in respect of any legal proceedings in the court"
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:4396 | (2) A court may, if satisfied that a party is conducting any legal
-- src:4397 | proceedings in the court in a vexatious manner, order that those
-- src:4398 | proceedings be stayed on such terms as the court considers
-- src:4399 | appropriate.
@ref s 73A(2) (src:4396-4399)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that a party is conducting the legal proceedings in a vexatious manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(2) the court may order the legal proceedings stayed on such terms as it considers appropriate` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF NOT `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any legal proceedings in the court"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that a party is conducting the legal proceedings in a vexatious manner`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that a party is conducting any legal proceedings in the court in a vexatious manner"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4403 | (3) A court may, if satisfied that the filing of further documents by a
-- src:4404 | party in any legal proceedings in the court would be vexatious or for
-- src:4411 | an improper purpose, order that no further documents be filed by that
-- src:4412 | party in relation to those proceedings.
@ref s 73A(3) (src:4403-4412)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party would be vexatious or for an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(3) the court may order that no further documents be filed by the party in relation to the legal proceedings` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF NOT `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in the court`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any legal proceedings in the court"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party would be vexatious or for an improper purpose`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party in any legal proceedings in the court would be vexatious or for an improper purpose"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4416 | (4) The General Division may, in respect of any legal proceedings
-- src:4417 | in any subordinate court —
-- src:4419 | (a) make a limited civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4420 | section 73B;
-- src:4422 | (b) make an extended civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4423 | section 73C; or
-- src:4425 | (c) make a general civil restraint order in accordance with
-- src:4426 | section 73D.
@ref s 73A(4) (src:4416-4426)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(4) the General Division may make a limited, extended or general civil restraint order in respect of the legal proceedings in a subordinate court` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "in respect of any legal proceedings in any subordinate court"
         ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:4430 | (5) The General Division may, if satisfied that a party is conducting
-- src:4431 | any legal proceedings in any subordinate court in a vexatious manner,
-- src:4432 | order that those proceedings be stayed on such terms as the General
-- src:4433 | Division considers appropriate.
@ref s 73A(5) (src:4430-4433)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division is satisfied that a party is conducting the legal proceedings in a vexatious manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(5) the General Division may order the legal proceedings in a subordinate court stayed on such terms as it considers appropriate` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF NOT `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any legal proceedings in any subordinate court"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the General Division is satisfied that a party is conducting the legal proceedings in a vexatious manner`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that a party is conducting any legal proceedings in any subordinate court in a vexatious manner"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4437 | (6) The General Division may, if satisfied that the filing of further
-- src:4438 | documents by a party in any legal proceedings in any subordinate
-- src:4439 | court would be vexatious or for an improper purpose, order that no
-- src:4440 | further documents be filed by that party in relation to those
-- src:4441 | proceedings.
@ref s 73A(6) (src:4437-4441)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division is satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party would be vexatious or for an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(6) the General Division may order that no further documents be filed by the party in relation to the legal proceedings in a subordinate court` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF NOT `the legal proceedings are legal proceedings in a subordinate court`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any legal proceedings in any subordinate court"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the General Division is satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party would be vexatious or for an improper purpose`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that the filing of further documents by a party in any legal proceedings in any subordinate court would be vexatious or for an improper purpose"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4445 | (7) A court may, on the court’s own motion, or on the application
-- src:4446 | of —
-- src:4448 | (a) the Attorney‑General; or
-- src:4450 | (b) any party in any legal proceedings in the court,
-- src:4452 | make an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)
-- src:4453 | against another party in those legal proceedings after giving the other
-- src:4454 | party an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 73A(7) (src:4445-4454)
-- "after giving the other party an opportunity to be heard" is a condition of the power: until the other party has had the opportunity, the order cannot be made.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party in the legal proceedings in the court applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party has been given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(7) the court may make the order against the other party` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF NOT `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF NOT `the other party has been given an opportunity to be heard`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after giving the other party an opportunity to be heard"
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the court acts on its own motion` OR `the Attorney-General applies` OR `a party in the legal proceedings in the court applies`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court acts "on the court's own motion, or on the application of (a) the Attorney-General; or (b) any party in any legal proceedings in the court", and the text says nothing of an application by anyone else
                   ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:4458 | (8) The General Division may, on the application of —
-- src:4460 | (a) the Attorney‑General; or
-- src:4462 | (b) any party in any legal proceedings in a subordinate court,
-- src:4469 | make an order mentioned in subsection (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)
-- src:4470 | against another party in those legal proceedings after giving the other
-- src:4471 | party an opportunity to be heard.
@ref s 73A(8) (src:4458-4471)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party in the legal proceedings in a subordinate court applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party has been given an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(8) the General Division may make the order against the other party` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF NOT `the order is one mentioned in subsection (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF NOT `the other party has been given an opportunity to be heard`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after giving the other party an opportunity to be heard"
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the Attorney-General applies` OR `a party in the legal proceedings in a subordinate court applies`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (8) names an application by the Attorney-General or a party, and, unlike subsection (7), does not name the court's own motion
                   ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:4475 | (9) A party against whom the General Division makes an order
-- src:4476 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c),
-- src:4477 | (5) or (6) may appeal against the order only with the permission of the
-- src:4478 | court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C.
@ref s 73A(9) (src:4475-4478)
-- Seam 9 of PLAN.md is an input: `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` IS A MAYBE Court
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 73A(9) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against an order of the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 73A the court is the General Division` court
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)`
        THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about an order of the General Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4475 | (9) A party against whom the General Division makes an order
-- src:4476 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c),
-- src:4477 | (5) or (6) may appeal against the order only with the permission of the
-- src:4478 | court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C.
@ref s 73A(9) ("only with the permission") (src:4475-4478)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(9) the party may appeal against the order of the General Division without permission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 73A the court is the General Division` court
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may appeal against the order only with the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2), (3), (4)(a), (b) or (c), (5) or (6)"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about an order of the General Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4484 | (9A) A party against whom the Appellate Division makes an order
-- src:4485 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3) may appeal
-- src:4486 | against the order only with the permission of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 73A(9A) (src:4484-4486)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 73A(9A) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against an order of the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `Appellate Division` AND `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST `Court of Appeal`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)" made by the Appellate Division
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4484 | (9A) A party against whom the Appellate Division makes an order
-- src:4485 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3) may appeal
-- src:4486 | against the order only with the permission of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 73A(9A) ("only with the permission") (src:4484-4486)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(9A) the party may appeal against the order of the Appellate Division without permission` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `Appellate Division` AND `the order is one mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may appeal against the order only with the permission of the Court of Appeal"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c), (2) or (3)" made by the Appellate Division
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4492 | (10) In this section and sections 73B and 73C, “legal proceedings”
-- src:4493 | includes any proceedings, process, action, application or appeal in
-- src:4494 | any civil matter or quasi‑criminal matter.
@ref s 73A(10) (src:4492-4494)
DECLARE `s 73A(10) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 73A(10) proceedings`
    `s 73A(10) process`
    `s 73A(10) action`
    `s 73A(10) application`
    `s 73A(10) appeal`
    `s 73A(10) another kind of thing`

GIVEN kind IS A `s 73A(10) kind of thing`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(10) the thing is within legal proceedings for ss 73A, 73B and 73C` MEANS
    IF NOT (kind EQUALS `s 73A(10) another kind of thing`)
       AND (nature EQUALS `a civil proceeding` OR nature EQUALS `a quasi-criminal proceeding`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "legal proceedings" "includes" the things listed, in a civil matter or a quasi-criminal matter, and the text does not close the list
    ELSE NOTHING


§ `Section 73B: limited orders`

-- src:4500 | 73B.—(1) A court may, if satisfied that a party has made 2 or more
-- src:4501 | applications that are totally without merit, make a limited civil
-- src:4502 | restraint order against the party.
@ref s 73B(1) (src:4500-4502)
-- "2 or more" is the Act's own figure.
`s 73B(1) the Act's number of applications totally without merit` MEANS 2

GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the number of applications made by the party that the court is satisfied are totally without merit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(1) the court may make a limited civil restraint order against the party` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF `the number of applications made by the party that the court is satisfied are totally without merit` AT LEAST `s 73B(1) the Act's number of applications totally without merit`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that a party has made 2 or more applications that are totally without merit"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4506 | (2) Where a court makes a limited civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4507 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4509 | (a) is restrained from making any further application in the
-- src:4510 | legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made
-- src:4511 | without the permission of that court; and
-- src:4515 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4516 | party has the permission of that court to make that
-- src:4517 | application.
@ref s 73B(2)(a) (src:4506-4517)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is a further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(2)(a) the party may make the further application in the legal proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order` AND `the application is a further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on "any further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made", by the party against whom it is made
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is "without the permission of that court", and the text grants nothing where there is permission
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is restrained from making any further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made without the permission of that court"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4506 | (2) Where a court makes a limited civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4507 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4509 | (a) is restrained from making any further application in the
-- src:4510 | legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made
-- src:4511 | without the permission of that court; and
-- src:4515 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4516 | party has the permission of that court to make that
-- src:4517 | application.
@ref s 73B(2)(a) (the restraint) (src:4506-4517)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is a further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(2)(a) the restraint on making the further application applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes a limited civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... is restrained": with no such order the "Where" is unmet, so the restraint does not apply (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the application is a further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`
         THEN IF `the party has the permission of the court`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the restraint is "without the permission of that court", so with the permission the restraint does not apply (fork S3-B6)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on "any further application in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made"
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4506 | (2) Where a court makes a limited civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4507 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4509 | (a) is restrained from making any further application in the
-- src:4510 | legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made
-- src:4511 | without the permission of that court; and
-- src:4515 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4516 | party has the permission of that court to make that
-- src:4517 | application.
@ref s 73B(2)(b) (src:4506-4517)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court to make the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(2)(b) the party may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes a limited civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order": the "Where" is unmet when there is no such order (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court to make the application`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the party has the permission of that court"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4528 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order,
-- src:4529 | makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under
-- src:4530 | subsection (2)) in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order
-- src:4531 | is made without the permission of the court under subsection (2), that
-- src:4532 | application is to be treated as dismissed —
-- src:4534 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4536 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4537 | merits of that application.
@ref s 73B(3) (src:4528-4537)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(3) the application is to be treated as dismissed` MEANS
    IF `the party is subject to a limited civil restraint order`
       AND `the application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
       AND `the application is made in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`
       AND NOT `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order, makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)) in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made without the permission of the court under subsection (2)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4528 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order,
-- src:4529 | makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under
-- src:4530 | subsection (2)) in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order
-- src:4531 | is made without the permission of the court under subsection (2), that
-- src:4532 | application is to be treated as dismissed —
-- src:4534 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4536 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4537 | merits of that application.
@ref s 73B(3)(a) (src:4528-4537)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(3)(a) the court has to make a further order for the application to be treated as dismissed` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the court having to make any further order"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words are "that application is to be treated as ... without the court having to make any further order", and say nothing where the application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4528 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order,
-- src:4529 | makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under
-- src:4530 | subsection (2)) in the legal proceedings in respect of which the order
-- src:4531 | is made without the permission of the court under subsection (2), that
-- src:4532 | application is to be treated as dismissed —
-- src:4534 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4536 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4537 | merits of that application.
@ref s 73B(3)(b) (src:4528-4537)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(3)(b) any other party must be heard on the merits of the application` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the need for any other party to be heard on the merits of that application"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words say nothing where the application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4543 | (4) A limited civil restraint order —
-- src:4545 | (a) is limited to the particular legal proceedings in respect of
-- src:4546 | which the order is made; and
-- src:4548 | (b) remains in effect for the duration of the legal proceedings
-- src:4549 | in respect of which the order is made, unless the court
-- src:4550 | orders otherwise.
@ref s 73B(4) (src:4543-4550)
GIVEN `the other legal proceedings are the particular legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(4)(a) the order reaches the legal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the other legal proceedings are the particular legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the order "is limited to the particular legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made", and "limited to" says "only" in other words (fork S3-B5)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made are still continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered that the order does not remain in effect for the duration of the legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(4)(b) the order remains in effect` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered that the order does not remain in effect for the duration of the legal proceedings`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the order "remains in effect for the duration of the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made, unless the court orders otherwise": this function asks whether the order is still in effect, a status, and the "unless" is met (fork S3-B2)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made are still continuing`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the order "remains in effect for the duration of the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made", and the duration has ended
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4554 | (5) Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order
-- src:4555 | made by the General Division, applies for the permission of the court
-- src:4556 | under subsection (2), and the court refuses such permission, the party
-- src:4557 | may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to
-- src:4558 | which the appeal is to be made under section 29C.
-- src:4564 | (6) Where a party, who is subject to a limited civil restraint order
-- src:4565 | made by the Appellate Division, applies for the permission of the
-- src:4566 | court under subsection (2), and the court refuses such permission, the
-- src:4567 | party may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the
-- src:4568 | Court of Appeal.
@ref s 73B(5) and (6) (src:4554-4568)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` IS A MAYBE Court
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 73B(5) and (6) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the refusal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections are about a party whose application "for the permission of the court under subsection (2)" the court refuses
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER court
         WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST `Court of Appeal`
         WHEN `General Division` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
         WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of an order made by the General Division or by the Appellate Division
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(5) and (6) the party may appeal against the refusal without permission` MEANS
    IF `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
       AND (court EQUALS `General Division` OR court EQUALS `Singapore International Commercial Court` OR court EQUALS `Appellate Division`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C" and "only with the permission of the Court of Appeal"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of a refusal by the General Division or the Appellate Division
    ELSE NOTHING


§ `Section 73C: extended orders`

-- src:4581 | 73C.—(1) A court may, if satisfied that a party has persistently
-- src:4582 | commenced actions or made applications that are totally without
-- src:4583 | merit, make an extended civil restraint order against the party.
@ref s 73C(1) (src:4581-4583)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court is satisfied that the party has persistently commenced actions or made applications that are totally without merit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(1) the court may make an extended civil restraint order against the party` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF `the court is satisfied that the party has persistently commenced actions or made applications that are totally without merit`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that a party has persistently commenced actions or made applications that are totally without merit"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4587 | (2) Where a court makes an extended civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4588 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4590 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4591 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4592 | the order, concerning any matter involving, relating to,
-- src:4593 | touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in
-- src:4594 | respect of which the order is made, without the permission
-- src:4595 | of the court that made the order; and
-- src:4599 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4600 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4601 | make that application.
@ref s 73C(2)(a) (src:4587-4601)
GIVEN `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(2)(a) the party may commence the action or make the application` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order`
            AND `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`
            AND `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on actions and applications "in any court or subordinate court specified in the order, concerning any matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is "without the permission of the court that made the order", and the text grants nothing where there is permission
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is restrained from commencing any action or making any application ... without the permission of the court that made the order"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4587 | (2) Where a court makes an extended civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4588 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4590 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4591 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4592 | the order, concerning any matter involving, relating to,
-- src:4593 | touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in
-- src:4594 | respect of which the order is made, without the permission
-- src:4595 | of the court that made the order; and
-- src:4599 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4600 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4601 | make that application.
@ref s 73C(2)(a) (the restraint) (src:4587-4601)
GIVEN `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(2)(a) the restraint on commencing the action or making the application applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes an extended civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... is restrained": with no such order the "Where" is unmet, so the restraint does not apply (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (`the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`
             AND `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`)
         THEN IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the restraint is "without the permission of the court that made the order", so with the permission the restraint does not apply (fork S3-B6)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on actions and applications "in any court or subordinate court specified in the order", "concerning any matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made"
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4587 | (2) Where a court makes an extended civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4588 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4590 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4591 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4592 | the order, concerning any matter involving, relating to,
-- src:4593 | touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in
-- src:4594 | respect of which the order is made, without the permission
-- src:4595 | of the court that made the order; and
-- src:4599 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4600 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4601 | make that application.
@ref s 73C(2)(b) (src:4587-4601)
GIVEN `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order to make the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(2)(b) the party may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes an extended civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order": the "Where" is unmet when there is no such order (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order to make the application`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the party has the permission of the court that made the order"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4607 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to an extended civil restraint
-- src:4608 | order, commences an action or makes an application (other than for
-- src:4609 | the permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4610 | subordinate court specified in the order, concerning any matter
-- src:4611 | involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal
-- src:4612 | proceedings in respect of which the order is made, without the
-- src:4613 | permission of the court under subsection (2), that action or
-- src:4614 | application is to be treated as struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4616 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4618 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4619 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73C(3) (src:4607-4619)
GIVEN `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(3) the action or application is to be treated as struck out or dismissed` MEANS
    IF `the party is subject to an extended civil restraint order`
       AND `the action or application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
       AND `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`
       AND `the action or application concerns a matter involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order is made`
       AND NOT `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party, who is subject to an extended civil restraint order, commences an action or makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or subordinate court specified in the order, ... without the permission of the court under subsection (2)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4607 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to an extended civil restraint
-- src:4608 | order, commences an action or makes an application (other than for
-- src:4609 | the permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4610 | subordinate court specified in the order, concerning any matter
-- src:4611 | involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal
-- src:4612 | proceedings in respect of which the order is made, without the
-- src:4613 | permission of the court under subsection (2), that action or
-- src:4614 | application is to be treated as struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4616 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4618 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4619 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73C(3)(a) (src:4607-4619)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(3)(a) the court has to make a further order for the action or application to be treated as struck out or dismissed` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the court having to make any further order"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words are "that action or application is to be treated as ... without the court having to make any further order", and say nothing where the action or application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4607 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to an extended civil restraint
-- src:4608 | order, commences an action or makes an application (other than for
-- src:4609 | the permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4610 | subordinate court specified in the order, concerning any matter
-- src:4611 | involving, relating to, touching upon or leading to the legal
-- src:4612 | proceedings in respect of which the order is made, without the
-- src:4613 | permission of the court under subsection (2), that action or
-- src:4614 | application is to be treated as struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4616 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4618 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4619 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73C(3)(b) (src:4607-4619)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(3)(b) any other party must be heard on the merits of the action or application` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the need for any other party to be heard on the merits of that action or application"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words say nothing where the action or application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4625 | (4) An extended civil restraint order —
-- src:4627 | (a) remains in effect for a period (not exceeding 2 years) that is
-- src:4628 | specified in the order; and
-- src:4635 | (b) must specify every court or subordinate court in which the
-- src:4636 | party against whom the order is made is restrained from
-- src:4637 | commencing any action or making any application.
@ref s 73C(4) (src:4625-4637)
GIVEN `the day the order takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day the order is to stop having effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(4)(a) the period specified in the order is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the day the order is to stop having effect` LESS THAN (`add years` `the day the order takes effect` `the Act's number of years for ss 73C(4)(a) and 73D(4)(a)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "remains in effect for a period (not exceeding 2 years) that is specified in the order"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(4)(b) the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the order "must specify every court or subordinate court in which the party against whom the order is made is restrained from commencing any action or making any application", and the text does not say what follows when it does not (fork S3-F7)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4641 | (5) The court —
-- src:4643 | (a) may extend the period for which an extended civil restraint
-- src:4644 | order remains in effect, if the court considers it appropriate
-- src:4645 | to do so; but
-- src:4647 | (b) must not extend that period for more than 2 years on any
-- src:4648 | given occasion.
@ref s 73C(5) (src:4641-4648)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is an extended civil restraint order in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(5)(a) the court may extend the period for which the order remains in effect` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF NOT `the order is an extended civil restraint order in effect`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the period for which an extended civil restraint order remains in effect"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may extend the period ..., if the court considers it appropriate to do so"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- The extension begins on the day after the period ends; "more than 2 years on any given occasion" is compared as for subsection (4)(a).
GIVEN `the day the period ends before the extension` IS A DATE
      `the day the period is to end after the extension` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(5)(b) the extension is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the day the period is to end after the extension` LESS THAN (`add years` (`the day the period ends before the extension` + 1) `the Act's number of years for ss 73C(4)(a) and 73D(4)(a)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the court "must not extend that period for more than 2 years on any given occasion"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4652 | (6) Where a party, who is subject to an extended civil restraint order
-- src:4653 | made by the General Division, applies for the permission of the court
-- src:4654 | under subsection (2), and the court refuses such permission, the party
-- src:4655 | may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to
