      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` IS A MAYBE Court
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 73C(6) and (7) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the refusal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections are about a party whose application "for the permission of the court under subsection (2)" the court refuses
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER court
         WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST `Court of Appeal`
         WHEN `General Division` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
         WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of an order made by the General Division or by the Appellate Division
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73C(6) and (7) the party may appeal against the refusal without permission` MEANS
    IF `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
       AND (court EQUALS `General Division` OR court EQUALS `Singapore International Commercial Court` OR court EQUALS `Appellate Division`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C" and "only with the permission of the Court of Appeal"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of a refusal by the General Division or the Appellate Division
    ELSE NOTHING


§ `Section 73D: general orders`

-- src:4674 | 73D.—(1) A court may, if satisfied that a party has persisted in
-- src:4675 | commencing actions or making applications that are totally without
-- src:4676 | merit, in circumstances where an extended civil restraint order would
-- src:4677 | not be sufficient or appropriate, make a general civil restraint order
-- src:4678 | against the party.
@ref s 73D(1) (src:4674-4678)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court is satisfied that the party has persisted in commencing actions or making applications that are totally without merit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an extended civil restraint order would not be sufficient or appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(1) the court may make a general civil restraint order against the party` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF `the court is satisfied that the party has persisted in commencing actions or making applications that are totally without merit`
            AND `an extended civil restraint order would not be sufficient or appropriate`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if satisfied that a party has persisted in commencing actions or making applications that are totally without merit, in circumstances where an extended civil restraint order would not be sufficient or appropriate"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4682 | (2) Where a court makes a general civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4683 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4685 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4686 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4693 | the order, without the permission of the court that made the
-- src:4694 | order; and
-- src:4698 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4699 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4700 | make that application.
@ref s 73D(2)(a) (src:4682-4700)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(2)(a) the party may commence the action or make the application` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the party is subject to a general civil restraint order` AND `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on actions and applications "in any court or subordinate court specified in the order"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is "without the permission of the court that made the order", and the text grants nothing where there is permission
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is restrained from commencing any action or making any application, in any court or subordinate court specified in the order, without the permission of the court that made the order"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4682 | (2) Where a court makes a general civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4683 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4685 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4686 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4693 | the order, without the permission of the court that made the
-- src:4694 | order; and
-- src:4698 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4699 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4700 | make that application.
@ref s 73D(2)(a) (the restraint) (src:4682-4700)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(2)(a) the restraint on commencing the action or making the application applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes a general civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... is restrained": with no such order the "Where" is unmet, so the restraint does not apply (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`
         THEN IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the restraint is "without the permission of the court that made the order", so with the permission the restraint does not apply (fork S3-B6)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on actions and applications "in any court or subordinate court specified in the order"
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4682 | (2) Where a court makes a general civil restraint order, the party
-- src:4683 | against whom the order is made —
-- src:4685 | (a) is restrained from commencing any action or making any
-- src:4686 | application, in any court or subordinate court specified in
-- src:4693 | the order, without the permission of the court that made the
-- src:4694 | order; and
-- src:4698 | (b) may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the
-- src:4699 | party has the permission of the court that made the order to
-- src:4700 | make that application.
@ref s 73D(2)(b) (src:4682-4700)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court that made the order to make the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(2)(b) the party may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court makes a general civil restraint order, the party against whom the order is made ... may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order": the "Where" is unmet when there is no such order (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the party has the permission of the court that made the order to make the application`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to amend, vary or discharge the order, only if the party has the permission of the court that made the order"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4706 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order,
-- src:4707 | commences an action or makes an application (other than for the
-- src:4708 | permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4709 | subordinate court specified in the order, without the permission of the
-- src:4710 | court under subsection (2), that action or application is to be treated as
-- src:4711 | struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4713 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4715 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4716 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73D(3) (src:4706-4716)
GIVEN `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(3) the action or application is to be treated as struck out or dismissed` MEANS
    IF `the party is subject to a general civil restraint order`
       AND `the action or application is other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
       AND `the action or application is in a court or subordinate court specified in the order`
       AND NOT `the party has the permission of the court under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order, commences an action or makes an application (other than for the permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or subordinate court specified in the order, ... without the permission of the court under subsection (2)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4706 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order,
-- src:4707 | commences an action or makes an application (other than for the
-- src:4708 | permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4709 | subordinate court specified in the order, without the permission of the
-- src:4710 | court under subsection (2), that action or application is to be treated as
-- src:4711 | struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4713 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4715 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4716 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73D(3)(a) (src:4706-4716)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(3)(a) the court has to make a further order for the action or application to be treated as struck out or dismissed` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the court having to make any further order"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words are "that action or application is to be treated as ... without the court having to make any further order", and say nothing where the action or application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4706 | (3) Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order,
-- src:4707 | commences an action or makes an application (other than for the
-- src:4708 | permission of the court under subsection (2)), in any court or
-- src:4709 | subordinate court specified in the order, without the permission of the
-- src:4710 | court under subsection (2), that action or application is to be treated as
-- src:4711 | struck out or dismissed —
-- src:4713 | (a) without the court having to make any further order; and
-- src:4715 | (b) without the need for any other party to be heard on the
-- src:4716 | merits of that action or application.
@ref s 73D(3)(b) (src:4706-4716)
GIVEN treated IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(3)(b) any other party must be heard on the merits of the action or application` MEANS
    CONSIDER treated
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the need for any other party to be heard on the merits of that action or application"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the words say nothing where the action or application is not so treated
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4722 | (4) A general civil restraint order —
-- src:4724 | (a) remains in effect for a period (not exceeding 2 years) that is
-- src:4725 | specified in the order; and
-- src:4727 | (b) must specify every court or subordinate court in which the
-- src:4728 | party against whom the order is made is restrained from
-- src:4729 | commencing any action or making any application.
@ref s 73D(4) (src:4722-4729)
GIVEN `the day the order takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day the order is to stop having effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(4)(a) the period specified in the order is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the day the order is to stop having effect` LESS THAN (`add years` `the day the order takes effect` `the Act's number of years for ss 73C(4)(a) and 73D(4)(a)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "remains in effect for a period (not exceeding 2 years) that is specified in the order"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(4)(b) the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the order specifies every court or subordinate court in which the party is restrained from commencing any action or making any application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the order "must specify every court or subordinate court in which the party against whom the order is made is restrained from commencing any action or making any application", and the text does not say what follows when it does not (fork S3-F7)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4733 | (5) The court —
-- src:4735 | (a) may extend the period for which a general civil restraint
-- src:4736 | order remains in effect, if the court considers it appropriate
-- src:4737 | to do so; but
-- src:4739 | (b) must not extend that period for more than 2 years on any
-- src:4740 | given occasion.
@ref s 73D(5) (src:4733-4740)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is a general civil restraint order in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(5)(a) the court may extend the period for which the order remains in effect` MEANS
    `s 73A the answer holds where the court is within the section` (`s 73A the court is a court within the section` court)
        (IF NOT `the order is a general civil restraint order in effect`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "the period for which a general civil restraint order remains in effect"
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the court considers it appropriate to extend the period`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may extend the period ..., if the court considers it appropriate to do so"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- The extension begins on the day after the period ends; "more than 2 years on any given occasion" is compared as for subsection (4)(a).
GIVEN `the day the period ends before the extension` IS A DATE
      `the day the period is to end after the extension` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(5)(b) the extension is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the day the period is to end after the extension` LESS THAN (`add years` (`the day the period ends before the extension` + 1) `the Act's number of years for ss 73C(4)(a) and 73D(4)(a)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the court "must not extend that period for more than 2 years on any given occasion"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4744 | (6) Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order
-- src:4745 | made by the General Division, applies for the permission of the court
-- src:4752 | under subsection (2), and the court refuses such permission, the party
-- src:4753 | may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to
-- src:4754 | which the appeal is to be made under section 29C.
-- src:4760 | (7) Where a party, who is subject to a general civil restraint order
-- src:4761 | made by the Appellate Division, applies for the permission of the
-- src:4762 | court under subsection (2), and the court refuses such permission, the
-- src:4763 | party may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the
-- src:4764 | Court of Appeal.
@ref s 73D(6) and (7) (src:4744-4764)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` IS A MAYBE Court
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 73D(6) and (7) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the refusal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections are about a party whose application "for the permission of the court under subsection (2)" the court refuses
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER court
         WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN JUST `Court of Appeal`
         WHEN `General Division` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
         WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of an order made by the General Division or by the Appellate Division
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73D(6) and (7) the party may appeal against the refusal without permission` MEANS
    IF `the court refused the party's application for permission under subsection (2)`
       AND (court EQUALS `General Division` OR court EQUALS `Singapore International Commercial Court` OR court EQUALS `Appellate Division`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may appeal against the refusal only with the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C" and "only with the permission of the Court of Appeal"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections speak of a refusal by the General Division or the Appellate Division
    ELSE NOTHING

